 r←Test_IE_006(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;ref;code;msg;orig;n1;n2;parms1;parms2
⍝ Test IE with an web page (Google). We need the user to search for something and click a link and judge success.
⍝ It would be really nice if we could automate this fully (SendKeys?!)
 r←∆Failed
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')

 :If batchFlag
     r←¯1
 :Else

     ⎕←(⎕PW-1)⍴'-'
     ⎕←'This test expects you to search for something via Google. The search page'
     ⎕←'should not change except by Ajax requests.'
     ⎕←'Please try and when you are sure it works that way then close the window.'
     ⎕←''
     ⎕←'Any link you click after a search should be displayed in your default browser.'
     ⎕←''
     ⎕←'To continue press <enter>'
     {}⍞

     parms1←#._APLGUI.GUI.StdForm.CreateParms
     parms1.caption←'IE Test Case Number "',(¯3↑↑⎕XSI),'"'
     n1←#._APLGUI.GUI.StdForm.Create parms1

     parms2←#._APLGUI.GUI.IE.CreateParms
     n2←parms2 #._APLGUI.GUI.IE.CreateIE n1.∆Form
     #._APLGUI.GUI.IE.Navigate n2.IEobject'http://google.com/'

     ⎕DQ n1.∆Form

     →PassesIf ∆AskQuestion'Did the Browser control act in the expected way? (y/n)'

     r←∆OK

 :EndIf

∆TidyUp:
 :Trap 0 ⋄ n.∆container.Close ⋄ :EndTrap
